  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity developed for strong public diplomacy</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOFA&apos;s strategic vision formulated</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To establish a digital platform to increase Saudi Representation in the UN system.
2) To Support the Department for Planning and Strategic Development.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A proposal was summitted to MOFA for the &#x201c;MoFA-UNDP Digital Platform; Building a Pathway to the United Nations.&#x201d; This was pitched as an interactive one stop shop for Saudi nationals to join the UN through digital tools. Phase I of its support to the Public Diplomacy Deputyship building on its work in 2020 in which a team of top experts in the field of Public Diplomacy delivered the following main outputs: a Functional Review, Development Plan, Benchmarking Report, Team Charters, and a PDD Strategy Document</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for MoFA reform and restructuring, improving MoFA as a workplace for its Employees, and supporting capability for increase of Saudi representation in International Organizations</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Benchmarking Report on International Best Practices to Increase Representation at the UN was developed and submitted for approval. In addition Focus Group Study Report on Causes of Saudi Underrepresentation in the UN System was also prepared.
UNDP has provided high level strategic advice and specific deliverables for the overall project management of the development of the International Recruitment Platform. Deliverables have focused on the design and operationalisation of business processes which will ensure that the MoFA Platform will have a mirror system, tools and processes for Saudis to maximise their potential for jobs in UNDP. Some examples of deliverables include &#x2013; career stream structures, competencies templates, selection methodologies, interview guides, career guidance tools, learning products, retention strategy and institutional support mechanisms.
UNDP has delivered a range of wrap around specialised digital services through the review and provision of technical advice/feedback on all major technical documentations, including but not limited to Process Model RD011, Statement of Work, AN 100 Analysis Specification for the MoFA International Recruitment Platform. UNDP has also provided specific technical inputs, content development, design support and problem solving solutions for the MoFA website.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A public diplomacy diagnostic conducted and a concrete road map for strategic and organizational change formulated 

Support to Improving MoFA Internal Structure and Capability provided 

The department for managing the Deployment of Saudi Nationals into the United Nations Agencies/Missions and into International Organizations strengthened</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Draft Public Diplomacy Strategy, Organizational Chart, Operating Models produced 

High-level assessment at the Ministry level undertaken and concluded with a set of practical recommendations for implementation 

A draft AWP to support the work of the General Department for Strategic Planning and Development endorsed and its implementation commenced through various constituent projects 

A draft proposal for increasing Saudis in the UN System endorsed and an AWP drafted for further discussion and endorsement

Sources:

&#x2022;	2020 AWP
&#x2022;	Endorsed Project Revision Document for SPDD
&#x2022;	2020 APR</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
